    "c67e27094e": {
      "id": "c67e27094e",
      "created": 1795241373.6912258,
      "headline": "Healy: Lombardia delay shows the power riders have on safety",
      "url": "https://www.cyclingnews.com/pro-cycling/safety/i-just-have-to-reiterate-the-power-that-we-have-as-riders-lombardia-protest-ringleader-ben-healy-emboldened-as-he-calls-for-change-on-rider-safety/",
      "source": "Cyclingnews",
      "image_url": "https://res.cloudinary.com/nnmxf7gb/image/upload/v1795241369/cycling-bot/c67e27094e-0.jpg",
      "image_urls": [
        "https://res.cloudinary.com/nnmxf7gb/image/upload/v1795241369/cycling-bot/c67e27094e-0.jpg",
        "https://res.cloudinary.com/nnmxf7gb/image/upload/v1795241370/cycling-bot/c67e27094e-1.jpg",
        "https://res.cloudinary.com/nnmxf7gb/image/upload/v1795241371/cycling-bot/c67e27094e-2.jpg",
        "https://res.cloudinary.com/nnmxf7gb/image/upload/v1795241372/cycling-bot/c67e27094e-3.jpg",
        "https://res.cloudinary.com/nnmxf7gb/image/upload/v1795241373/cycling-bot/c67e27094e-4.jpg"
      ],
      "full_caption": "Ben Healy says the five-minute delay at Il Lombardia was a clear message from the peloton on safety.\n\nThe EF Education-EasyPost rider was the driving force behind the 'stand' before the season's final Monument. It followed a series of near-misses at the Italian autumn Classics. Healy wants the UCI to listen and work with riders on change, rather than assign blame.\n\nShould riders delay races again if safety doesn't improve?\n\nSource: Cyclingnews\n\n#cycling #procycling #roadcycling #WorldTour #IlLombardia #BenHealy #EFEducationEasyPost #RiderSafety #UCI #cyclingnews",
      "alt_text": "News graphic with the headline about Ben Healy saying the Il Lombardia start delay showed the power riders have on safety.",
      "score": 6,
      "reel_url": null,
      "category": "RIDER NEWS",
      "slides": [
        {
          "title": "A five-minute stand at Lombardia",
          "text": "The peloton delayed the start of Il Lombardia, the season's last Monument, by five minutes. Ben Healy (EF Education-EasyPost) drove the action and calls it a 'stand' rather than a protest."
        },
        {
          "title": "Why riders acted",
          "text": "Safety has been a major topic since Finlay Tarling's death at the Volta a Portugal. Further near-misses followed at the Italian autumn Classics, including a police motorbike riding head-on toward the peloton at Tre Valli Varesine."
        },
        {
          "title": "Healy's message to the UCI",
          "text": "Healy says riders wanted to show what they can do if the problems continue. He hopes the UCI will listen and work with them, and says the aim is to be productive rather than point blame."
        },
        {
          "title": "What the UCI has done so far",
          "text": "After Tarling's death, the UCI's Professional Cycling Council discussed some safety issues. Healy says the cars on course in Italy showed that nothing had really changed."
        }
      ],
      "background_url": null,
      "text_message_id": 198
    },
    "d5ba7ceea8": {
      "id": "d5ba7ceea8",
      "created": 1795255801.2887325,
      "headline": "Carapaz leaning towards a Giro d'Italia return",
      "url": "https://news.google.?oc=5",
      "source": "CyclingUpToDate.com",
      "image_url": "https://res.cloudinary.com/nnmxf7gb/image/upload/v1795255800/cycling-bot/d5ba7ceea8-0.jpg",
      "image_urls": [
        "https://res.cloudinary.com/nnmxf7gb/image/upload/v1795255800/cycling-bot/d5ba7ceea8-0.jpg"
      ],
      "full_caption": "Richard Carapaz is leaning towards a return to the Giro d'Italia. 🇪🇨\n\nAccording to CyclingUpToDate, the Ecuadorian wants to target big wins in his upcoming programme. He also acknowledges that Tadej Pogacar is clearly a level above the rest of the peloton.\n\nNothing is final yet, as the report only says he is leaning towards the Giro. An official confirmation of his race schedule is still to come.\n\nCan Carapaz take a big win at the Giro, or is Pogacar too strong for everyone?\n\nSource: CyclingUpToDate\n\n#cycling #procycling #roadcycling #WorldTour #RichardCarapaz #GirodItalia #Giro #TadejPogacar #cyclingnews #peloton",
      "alt_text": "News graphic with the text 'Carapaz leaning towards a Giro d'Italia return' in the Cycling News Today style.",
      "score": 6,
      "reel_url": null,
      "category": "RIDER NEWS",
      "slides": [],
      "background_url": null,
      "text_message_id": 201
    },
    "83691951b0": {
      "id": "83691951b0",
      "created": 1795259393.700483,
      "headline": "Roglič to get a new coach for the first time as a pro",
      "url": "https://www.cyclingnews.com/pro-cycling/teams-riders/maybe-this-will-add-something-more-primoz-roglic-will-change-coach-for-the-first-time-in-his-career-following-move-to-nsn/",
      "source": "Cyclingnews",
      "image_url": "https://res.cloudinary.com/nnmxf7gb/image/upload/v1795259391/cycling-bot/83691951b0-0.jpg",
      "image_urls": [
        "https://res.cloudinary.com/nnmxf7gb/image/upload/v1795259391/cycling-bot/83691951b0-0.jpg",
        "https://res.cloudinary.com/nnmxf7gb/image/upload/v1795259392/cycling-bot/83691951b0-1.jpg",
        "https://res.cloudinary.com/nnmxf7gb/image/upload/v1795259392/cycling-bot/83691951b0-2.jpg",
        "https://res.cloudinary.com/nnmxf7gb/image/upload/v1795259393/cycling-bot/83691951b0-3.jpg"
      ],
      "full_caption": "Primož Roglič is set to work with a new coach for the first time in his career.\n\nCyclingnews understands that long-time coach Marc Lamberts will not follow him to NSN Cycling. Slovenia's national coach Uroš Murn points to Tadej Pogačar's coaching switch as a sign that a change can help. NSN has not yet said who will coach Roglič in 2027.\n\nCan a new coach bring something extra from Roglič at 37?\n\nSource: Cyclingnews\n\n#cycling #procycling #roadcycling #WorldTour #PrimozRoglic #Roglic #NSNCycling #RedBullBora #cyclingnews #cyclingtransfers",
      "alt_text": "News graphic with the headline that Primož Roglič will have a new coach for the first time in his professional career after joining NSN Cycling.",
      "score": 7,
      "reel_url": null,
      "category": "RIDER NEWS",
      "slides": [
        {
          "title": "Lamberts stays at Red Bull",
          "text": "Cyclingnews understands Marc Lamberts will not follow Primož Roglič to NSN Cycling. He is set to remain on the coaching staff at Red Bull-Bora-Hansgrohe in 2027."
        },
        {
          "title": "A partnership since 2016",
          "text": "Lamberts has coached Roglič since he turned pro with LottoNL-Jumbo in 2016, and moved with him to Red Bull in 2024. Roglič, 37, joins NSN on a one-year contract."
        },
        {
          "title": "The Pogačar example",
          "text": "Slovenia coach Uroš Murn cited Pogačar's 2024 switch from Iñigo San Millán to Javier Sola, saying Roglič has nothing to lose. NSN has not confirmed who will coach him in 2027."
        }
      ],
      "background_url": null,
      "text_message_id": 213
    },
